<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">García Ramírez of Navarre</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1112–1150</span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a> · Also known as García the Restorer, García Ramírez the Restorer</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">García Ramírez, called the Restorer, was King of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-navarre">Navarre</a> from 1134 to 1150. On the death of Alfonso the Battler, who had ruled both Aragon and Navarre, the Navarrese nobles chose him as king, restoring Navarre's independence. He became a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vassal">vassal</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alfonso-vii-of-leon-and-castile">Alfonso VII of Castile</a> and joined his campaign against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/almeria">Almería</a> in 1147.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/garcia-ramirez-of-navarre.jpg" alt="García Ramírez of Navarre" width="317" height="568" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Garcia_(IV)_Ramires_de_Navarra_-_Compendio_de_cr%C3%B3nicas_de_reyes_(Biblioteca_Nacional_de_Espa%C3%B1a).png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
